From: Yeye B.B.C. <19569343+yeyebbc@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: Vote the TB522FU UFS ref-clock supply

The factory board tree connects the UFS device reference-clock pad to
PMIC i LDO2 at 1.2 V. The stock UFS host enables this supply at probe
and retains it through Hibern8. The mainline board has no LDO2 node.

Use an RPMh always-on constraint to make the vote available in the boot
kernel before it loads the hibernation image. Keep the existing SDB
and Hibern8 settings for the comparison. The extra vote is a diagnostic
until protected firmware restore establishes its effect.

Signed-off-by: Yeye B.B.C. <19569343+yeyebbc@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8750-lenovo-y900-acm.dts | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8750-lenovo-y900-acm.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8750-lenovo-y900-acm.dts
index 6f87a5328ad2da31d5cca97c77e538e9559c1453..88c3720483d8d21562ae171d5c5a61338959e1c1 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8750-lenovo-y900-acm.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8750-lenovo-y900-acm.dts
@@ -88,6 +88,14 @@ regulators-i {
   compatible = "qcom,pm8550ve-rpmh-regulators"; qcom,pmic-id = "i";
   vdd-s7-supply = <&vph_pwr>;
   vreg_s7i: smps7 { regulator-name = "vreg_s7i"; regulator-min-microvolt = <1224000>; regulator-max-microvolt = <1340000>; regulator-initial-mode = <RPMH_REGULATOR_MODE_HPM>; };
+		/* Stock UFS device reference-clock pad supply. */
+		ldo2 {
+			regulator-name = "vreg_l2i_ufs_refclk";
+			regulator-min-microvolt = <1200000>;
+			regulator-max-microvolt = <1200000>;
+			regulator-initial-mode = <RPMH_REGULATOR_MODE_HPM>;
+			regulator-always-on;
+		};
   vreg_l3i: ldo3 { regulator-name = "vreg_l3i_dsi"; regulator-min-microvolt = <880000>; regulator-max-microvolt = <912000>; regulator-initial-mode = <RPMH_REGULATOR_MODE_HPM>; };
  };
  regulators-j {
